COPY public.testimonials (id, "memberName", role, quote, category, photo, active, "order", "createdAt") FROM stdin;
2a0ea958-0fc7-4377-baeb-0658af2017f8	Emma L.	Relocated from Paris	I joined Smileys two weeks after moving to Istanbul with zero contacts. By the end of my first month I had dinner plans four nights a week. I genuinely don't know what my life here would look like without it.	expat	\N	t	1	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
293b7b67-4517-42c2-857e-adc3c3d37889	David K.	Software engineer	I'm not naturally a social person. Big parties and networking events drain me. Smileys was different from day one — smaller groups, real conversations, no pressure. It's the first community I've ever actually stayed in.	friends	\N	t	2	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
adce0d29-ee8e-4d9d-b360-84868e208c59	Nadia R.	Architect	I met my business partner at a Smileys dinner. Six months later we won our first project together. Some of the best professional decisions I've made started as a conversation at one of these events.	business	\N	t	3	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
4474b382-75d0-4642-b9ec-f95740177580	Tom W.	Digital nomad	I've used Meetup, Internations, Facebook groups — none of them come close. The people here actually show up, actually engage, and actually remember your name the next time. That's rare.	general	\N	t	4	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
c19006c8-fd96-477d-8044-8824c8af32d0	Ayşe M.	Local member	As someone who grew up in Istanbul, I thought I already had my circle. Smileys showed me a side of my own city I had never seen — through the eyes of people discovering it for the first time. Now my closest friends are from six different countries.	friends	\N	t	5	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
92348da7-e194-431f-9d8a-98fe08fc1636	Marco F.	Entrepreneur	I came for a sailing trip with strangers. I left with three people I'd genuinely call friends. That's the Smileys effect — it creates the conditions for real connection and then gets out of the way.	travel	\N	t	6	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
4383a68a-e909-4c15-912d-f93b86e2b466	Priya S.	UX designer	The French Meetup was the first event I attended. I showed up alone, nervous, not even sure my French was good enough. An hour in I forgot I was nervous. That's what a good community does — it makes showing up feel safe.	general	\N	t	7	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
4bf87e7f-663d-4d40-bf8f-02e4f7523a50	Chris B.	Remote worker from Berlin	Three months in Istanbul on a remote year. Smileys turned what could have been a lonely stretch into one of the best periods of my life. I extended my stay twice because of the people I met here.	expat	\N	t	8	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
ef3e7314-6bb9-4271-a89a-6d26a5923223	Leila H.	Photographer	The photowalk changed my relationship with Istanbul completely. I'd walked those streets a hundred times and never really seen them. Sharing that experience with people who are genuinely curious — that's what made it special.	travel	\N	t	9	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
5e933cb9-91f9-4852-9562-8211830cf41e	James T.	Finance, moved from London	I was skeptical at first. I'd been burned by other 'community' groups that turned out to be just WhatsApp noise. Smileys is different. There's a real culture here — of showing up, being present, and actually caring about the people around you.	general	\N	t	10	2026-05-10 04:58:04.871
d827757f-4487-43a9-a6be-93fd4d708201	Sara K.	Member since 2023	I want to thank Nate, the founder of Smileys, for creating such a wonderful community. About two years ago I attended my first Smileys activity on International Women's Day. What I saw was full of kindness and support. Even though it was my first time meeting most of the people there, I felt like I was among sisters rather than strangers. Since then, I realized that Smileys is not just a group for activities — but a place that brings kind people together and creates real friendships and beautiful memories.	friends		t	0	2026-05-10 04:38:52.565
9da86230-eca3-46b7-83de-2280771b01fc	Hakan T.	Street photographer & club host	I first heard about Smileys at a language exchange event, where I shared my idea of starting a photography group. Someone mentioned Smileys and suggested I create my group there — that's how I became part of this community. I'm a street photographer, and Smileys has given me the chance to share my passion with people from different cultures. What I find particularly inspiring is how foreigners view Istanbul with fresh eyes. Through them, I've discovered details in the city I had never noticed before. Smileys has been more than just a platform for socialising — it's allowed me to meet people from various cultural backgrounds and engage in creative activities I truly enjoy. It's a refreshing alternative to the usual meetups, where conversations can feel drawn out over drinks in a bar. What keeps me anchored here is the mutual respect and strong sense of equality that everyone embodies. It's a rare quality that makes this community truly special.	friends	\N	t	1	2026-05-10 05:09:11.492
\.
